<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">African Agricultural Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Syndicat Agricole Africain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The African Agricultural Union (Syndicat Agricole Africain) was an association of African planters in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a> founded in 1944 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-houphouet-boigny">Félix Houphouët-Boigny</a>. It campaigned against forced labour, which favoured European planters, and against the unequal treatment of African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> and cocoa growers. Its network formed the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-party-uganda">Democratic Party</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">Ivory</a> Coast, founded in 1946, the year forced labour was abolished.</p></div>
